course: dictionary
lesson: 5465
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The words around «lapse» give the clues. A lapse can be a slip of memory, a short gap in time, or something that stops working because it was not renewed.
explain: «He had a memory lapse and forgot his lunch.» Lapse must mean a small slip, because a memory lapse is a moment when your memory lets you down. Try the swap: "He had a memory slip and forgot his lunch." It still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: «The stories lapse into silence when the lights go out.» Here lapse is a verb, meaning to slowly fall into a state. The word «into» is your clue: something has changed from one state to another, and the state is silence.
explain: «My library card lapsed because I did not renew it.» This lapse means the card stopped being valid. You can tell from «did not renew it», because the card ran out since nobody paid it again. Read on if you are unsure, and check the other words for clues.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Lapse as a noun means a small mistake or a short gap in time, such as «a lapse of memory» or «after a lapse of a few minutes».
fact: Lapse as a verb can mean to stop being valid, to slowly fall into a state like «lapse into silence», or to stop a habit you used to have.
fact: Phrases help: «a lapse in concentration» means a short loss of focus, and «a lapse in judgement» means a mistake from not thinking carefully.
fact: A good check is to swap a simpler word into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «He had a memory lapse and forgot his lunch.» What does lapse mean here? | A new school bag | A loud noise | A long holiday | *A small slip in remembering
exercise: «After a lapse of a few minutes, the rain started again.» What does lapse mean here? | A type of cloud | A big argument | A lost dog | *A short gap in time
exercise: «The stories lapse into silence when the lights go out.» What does lapse into silence mean? | Ran out of the room | *Slowly fell into silence | Shouted loudly | Sang a song
test: «My library card lapsed because I did not renew it.» What does lapsed mean here? | Was read aloud | Grew bigger | Was found again | *Stopped being valid
test: Which phrase names a small mistake caused by not thinking carefully? | A large prize | A kind sort of weather | A happy memory | *A lapse in judgement
exam: Lily says «lapse» always means a mistake. Is she right? | No, it means a type of dance | *No, it can also mean a short gap in time or something that stops being valid | Yes, it means a big party | Yes, it only ever means a mistake
